From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nobody <>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:08:32 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] perf: run Laya head layers on the GPU

The two head transformer layers ran on CPU after the GPU encode: ~60 ms of an
~85 ms decision. Run them as one ggml graph on the first GPU device for every
input of the request (matmuls batched across inputs, attention per input);
scorer and act head stay on CPU. LLAMA_LAYA_HEAD=cpu keeps the CPU path, and
any GPU failure falls back to it. Head ~62 ms -> ~7 ms on an RX 7900 XTX;
answers match the CPU head (max |dp| 1e-4, no flipped answers).
---
